# Java Enterprise Standards

## Code Quality
- All public methods MUST have Javadoc with @param, @return, @throws
- Use @Transactional for all service methods that modify data
- Validate all inputs using @Valid in controllers
- Use Lombok (@Data, @Builder) for DTOs to reduce boilerplate
- Implement custom exception hierarchy extending RuntimeException

## Architecture
- Follow layered architecture: Controller → Service → Repository
- Use DTOs for all API responses (never expose entities directly)
- Implement caching with @Cacheable for expensive operations
- Use Spring Profiles (dev, test, prod) for environment-specific config

## Security
- All endpoints require authentication unless explicitly allowed
- Use Spring Security with JWT
- Validate user permissions with @PreAuthorize
- Never log sensitive data (passwords, tokens, PII)

## Testing
- All service methods must have unit tests (JUnit 5 + Mockito)
- Controller tests using MockMvc
- Integration tests for critical flows
- Target 80% code coverage minimum
